  "sequentialJustification": {
    "kind": "caller-level-parallelism",
    "detail": "The FlatSQL store node appends records into a single arena whose write cursor is the serialization point; concurrent appends inside the guest would race that cursor and break the byte-identical persisted-state guarantee the tri-runtime parity contract depends on. Any parallelism is the caller's: the host may run independent store invocations against separate arenas, and the heavy query work runs in the engine's own AOT context outside this artifact."
  }
}
